"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T09:44:15Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T10:08:10Z","body":"So a few potential issues:\r\n* Containers use signed sizes, so it's relevant to check for sizing issues, I'd say it might be better to use signed sizes unless impossible (realized it all uses 32 bit numbers for unsigned so that shouldn't be a problem)\r\n* For putting functional code inside error macros that's something I've been wanting to discuss for our usage and style guides as I feel it'd be better to not put code that changes things inside macros in case we want to be able to remove the tests etc.\r\n\r\nWill go over style, but from a glance I don't think there's anything significant beyond that","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979683123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2980454301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-2980454301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":2980454301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xph-d","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T13:46:31Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:46:18Z","body":"> Containers use signed sizes\r\n\r\nMakes sense. Although realistically, that limit can never be reached unless the user has over 17 ***billion*** GB of RAM and storage. Assuming you would have the max possible values for channels (2^16) and mix rate (2^32) it would be enough to fit 18 hours of audio, but of course, the probability of a stream like this being created by someone is literally null.\r\n\r\n The data length now uses a signed 64-bit integer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2980454301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993286147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-2993286147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":2993286147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yaewD","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T03:21:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T03:21:29Z","body":"Modified a few more things that could have caused problems to playback (more `uint32_t` to `int64_t` conversions).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993286147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049645357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3049645357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3049645357,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61xeUt","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T16:48:50Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T16:48:50Z","body":"cc. @Ivorforce If you could review this PR, it's highly technical about integer types, if you can help us.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049645357/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049821636","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3049821636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3049821636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61yJXE","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T17:53:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T17:54:54Z","body":"> Containers use signed sizes, so it's relevant to check for sizing issues, I'd say it might be better to use signed sizes unless impossible (realized it all uses 32 bit numbers for unsigned so that shouldn't be a problem)\r\n\r\nSorry for bringing this up again, but this is incorrect. Both `LocalVector` and `Vector` use unsigned sizes internally. Some interfaces accept signed sizes to avoid accidental conversion of user-supplied negative values to unsigned, which would result in confusing error messages. Some interfaces also return signed sizes, either for consistency or just as legacy behavior. But internally, our containers are using unsigned sizes.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what was changed from this suggestion, but unsigned is appropriate when dealing with non-negative data. I'd suggest changing at least `TightLocalVector` to use `uint64_t`. Most other data types that were previously unsigned should probably remain so.\r\n\r\nGenerally, the change looks sensible to me, but implicit C++ conversions make it difficult to be very sure that nothing unintentional is happening. Unfortunately (afaik) it's impossible to be sure about it without testing. I'll review the code again in more detail when the above suggestions are addressed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049821636/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050220831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3050220831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3050220831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61zq0f","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T20:30:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T20:30:38Z","body":"> I'd suggest changing at least `TightLocalVector` to use `uint64_t`\r\n\r\nAddressed. Also took the opportunity to modify some missing changes.\r\n\r\nNote that getting the length in `_mix_internal` needs to use a signed integer, as it triggers a warning due to a comparison with `offset`, which needs to be able to be negative (or else we would need a bigger refactor).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050220831/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3052895892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3052895892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3052895892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61936U","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T14:31:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T14:31:19Z","body":"Following @Ivorforce suggestion, I moved the milestone to 4.6.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3052895892/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053364480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3053364480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3053364480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61_qUA","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T16:59:16Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T17:09:54Z","body":"If there is any regressions, those would only be noticeable if we tried to import a 2GB+ WAV file, as that's where the range of signed 32-bit int overflows.\r\n\r\nIf you do try importing a 2GB+ file right now, the import will be broken because it will try to assign `UINT32_MAX` to a signed `int`. This won't happen with this PR in.\r\n\r\nAlso, I don't think wrapping a 64-bit data range with a signed integer (there is only *one* iteration of that, as Ivorforce complained, that isn't a default from a WAV file) breaks anything, as the average storage/RAM doesn't cover that much range, and I doubt it will before hundreds of years.\r\n\r\nThere are some sign changes I could revert that wouldn't make a problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3053364480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3054044747","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3054044747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3054044747,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62CQZL","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-09T21:10:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-09T21:11:24Z","body":"> If there is any regressions, those would only be noticeable if we tried to import a 2GB+ WAV file, as that's where the range of signed 32-bit int overflows.\r\n\r\nI'm specifically worried about breaking normal files by implicit conversions, not just 2GB+ files. Changing types like this can break math in unexpected ways. \r\n\r\n> There are some sign changes I could revert that wouldn't make a problem.\r\n\r\nI think your PR is fine as is.\r\nI'm not _against_ a 4.5 merge, I just wouldn't vouch for it since the release is getting quite close. Since loading >2Gb files is kind of niché, I think the fix can wait to reduce regression risks. We can still cherry-pick it once it's been under test for a bit in alpha.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3054044747/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303759681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#issuecomment-3303759681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107596","id":3303759681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E619B","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T16:30:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T16:30:12Z","body":"Needs rebase","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3303759681/reacti